---
deadlock_detection: true
options:
  max_actions: 400
  crash_on_yield: false
---
# views.fizz -- a fizzbee model of how a pool's workers come by their views of
# chisel's cache during one Pass: the probing view, the workers that wait for
# it, views seeded in part ("thin") and made whole, a blob fetched again, and
# a cut that is cut again in a whole view. pool.go and ../cache/cache.go are
# the code; this is not a transcription of them and proves nothing of them
# line by line. It checks the protocol they are meant to follow.
#
# five configurations, since one of everything is more states than the
# checker gets through (480k and counting after 25 minutes):
#   views (as written): two groups of a lead and one unit, no group is
#     stopped, every outcome and need. Retry, a blob fetched again, views
#     made whole, the probe. 27485 states.
#   stops: one group of a lead and two units and a lone lead, one stop,
#     clean cuts but for what they need. The skip, the prober that cuts
#     nothing (D1), letting go. 102344 states.
#   later: as stops with a unit after the second lead and no old blob
#     needed: the prober that let go cuts again. 30468 states.
#   kept: as views with clean cuts, and a view that may lack nothing
#     though seeded in part, as one kept from an earlier run may: it
#     neither probes nor waits. 21421 states.
#   kept4: four workers and three lone leads, a view that may lack
#     nothing, no old blob needed: two views seeded in part behind one
#     that lacks nothing (D3). 30375 states.
#
# run:   make fizz    (the five, and the three designs that must fail)
# by hand, fizzbee 0.5.4:
#   timeout -k 10 600 fizz views.fizz
#   timeout -k 10 600 fizz --preinit-hook "$STOPS" views.fizz
# with STOPS the lines   GROUPS = [2, 0]   MAX_STOPS = 1   KINDS = ["ok"]
# later is GROUPS = [2, 1] and a line more, NEEDS = ["recent"]. A design
# that must fail is the stops configuration and a line more:
#   FIX = "none"      a deadlock: the pass hangs (R2)
#   FIX = "release"   fails R3
# kept is KINDS = ["ok"] and SEEDS = ["thin", "whole"]; kept4 is W = 4,
# GROUPS = [0, 0, 0], KINDS = ["ok"], NEEDS = ["recent"] and that SEEDS.
# The third design that must fail is kept4 and a line more:
#   ORDER = "decide_first"   fails R3
#
# requirements
#
# R1:  THE POOL SHALL hand every unit it cuts to the caller once, with the
#      result the unit has on its own: what the cut does in a view of every
#      blob the shared cache had when the view was seeded. It never hands
#      on a failure for such a blob the view lacked.
# R2:  THE POOL SHALL finish a pass: every worker ends, whatever the units
#      need, the network does and the caller answers, as long as every cut
#      and every callback returns.
# R3:  WHILE no view seeded in part has cut a unit and merged, THE POOL
#      SHALL let no second view seeded in part cut.
# R4:  IF the probing view's first cut lacked a blob the shared cache had,
#      THEN THE POOL SHALL let no other view cut while it is seeded in
#      part.
# R5:  WHEN a worker has seen that views are to be whole, THE POOL SHALL
#      not cut in that worker's view while it is seeded in part.
# R6:  THE POOL SHALL let at most one cut a worker lack a blob the shared
#      cache had when the worker's view was seeded.
# R7:  THE POOL SHALL skip a unit only when its group was stopped, and
#      once views are to be whole they stay so.
#
# invariants: R1, R3, R4, R5, R6, R7. progress: R2. R1 is also read at the
# end of the pass, where every unit is cut, skipped or was never queued.
#
# the boundary
#
# system: the workers' loop of Pass, worker.prepare, cut, whole, merge,
# proved and close, and the pool's whole flag and probed channel.
# environment: what a unit needs (a blob used of late, or an old one the
# shared cache has), what the unit's own cut does (ok, a failure of its
# own, a failure for what the archives hold), the network (up or down, as
# it likes, read once by each cut), and the caller stopping a unit's group.
#
# assumptions, each a thing the code can meet and the model does not
#
# - a fresh pool with a positive window: no view is left from an earlier
#   pass, so every worker's view comes from the cache. That one may be a
#   view kept from an earlier run (../cache/kept.fizz is how a run comes
#   by it): it has what it had then and what was used of late since, so
#   it lacks old blobs or, made whole back then, lacks none.
# - every cut and every callback returns.
# - the shared cache only grows during the pass: a blob it has stays. So a
#   blob it had at the start is "of late" or "old" for the whole pass. A
#   blob another worker fetches and merges during the pass is in no view
#   seeded before, thin or whole, and Complete does not bring it: a cut
#   needing it fetches it for itself, as it always did in a view, and that
#   is the unit's own outcome here, not a blob the view lacked.
# - the cache's links succeed and the view is on the shared cache's
#   filesystem: Complete makes a view that lacks nothing. A link that
#   fails otherwise, or a view that copies, is a view lacking blobs that
#   says it is whole, and a cut in it fetches or fails as chisel does in
#   any cache.
# - a unit's own outcome is the same each time it is cut in a view of
#   every blob, and the archives say the same thing all pass.
#
# abstractions
#
# - GROUPS groups, each a lead and so many units after it. A lead is never
#   skipped. The second group has a unit after its lead so that a worker
#   whose unit of the first was skipped has something left to cut.
# - worker 0 cuts in the shared cache and has no view. The others are
#   isolated and get a view on their first unit.
# - a view is "thin" (seeded in part and lacking the old blobs) or "whole".
#   A thin view that happens to lack nothing is a whole one here: SEEDS is
#   what seeding in part may give, "thin" alone when every view is made
#   new and alike, "whole" too when a kept view may lack nothing.
# - a unit cut in the shared cache or in a whole view is "ok": its own
#   failures take no branch of the protocol there. In a thin view it is
#   "ok" or "bad", a failure of its own, which is cut again. A failure for
#   what the archives hold is not cut again and goes the way of "ok".
# - a blob fetched again is a flag on the view until the merge sees it, or
#   until Complete links the blob in and the merge no longer can.
#
# what an atomic step merges
#
# every step of a worker is one atomic block of the one Step action, a
# worker picked without order among those that can move. A step holds at
# most one read or write of what workers share (the queue and its count,
# stopped, whole, probed), or several that no other worker's step can come
# between to any effect; what else it does is the worker's own. Each stands
# for:
# - take: one receive from the queue.
# - prepare: the first p.mu section of prepare, where whole is read for
#   the window, then p.seeding held over cache.NewRecent. The view is the
#   worker's own until it has it, and what NewRecent reads of the shared
#   cache is fixed by the assumption above. whole turning true during the
#   seeding is read again at the gate.
# - gate: the second p.mu section, for a view that lacks blobs: whole and
#   probed read, and probed made by the first to come. A worker that sees
#   whole true has its view made whole before it cuts, which is the cut
#   step's Complete, the view being its own.
# - wait: the receive from probed, then whole(false), which reads whole
#   under p.mu and Completes the worker's own view.
# - skipcheck: the pm section reading stopped. A worker whose view is not
#   seeded in part goes from here to done: its cut reads and writes
#   nothing shared.
# - cut: whole(false), then one chisel in the view, start to end, and
#   cuts set. whole(false) reads p.whole under p.mu, drops the lock, and
#   Completes the worker's own view; the chisel then runs in it. The one
#   shared read is of whole, at the start: whoever sets whole later is
#   after the step, which is the code's "before its next cut". The
#   network is read once, by the chisel. What a chisel does in its own
#   view no one sees until the merge.
# - retry: whole(true), p.whole set under p.mu, then Complete, then the
#   second chisel. The one shared write is of whole, at the start; the
#   rest is in the worker's own view, by now whole, where no blob is
#   lacking and the network is not asked.
# - done: the caller's callback and the pm section setting stopped. The
#   callback does nothing here but decide, so its place is the set.
# - merge: View.Merge, then the p.mu section of merge setting whole.
#   Merge's links into the shared cache are the growth assumed above, and
#   what it finds is the worker's own.
# - enditem: proved, the close of the channel, then the last pm section
#   of the loop with its sends to the queue. A worker let go by the close
#   reads whole and seeds, a worker at the queue reads the queue: neither
#   reads what the other half writes. Merging them does fix an order the
#   code leaves open, of this worker's sends against those of a worker
#   let go that ends its unit first: which unit a worker gets and when a
#   callback comes, on which no requirement here stands. A worker
#   receiving a unit before pending is counted cannot end its own unit
#   until pm is free.
# - close: worker.close: its merge, which finds nothing new since every
#   unit was merged, proved, and the view handed back.
# merge and enditem are two steps on purpose: whole set, then probed
# closed, is the order R3 and R4 stand on.
#
# not modelled: the context being cancelled, a view that cannot be made, a
# second Pass reusing the views, Serial, the sizing of a pass, and what the
# assumptions above set aside.
#
# decisions the model forced
#
# D1: a probing worker whose unit is skipped, its group stopped while the
#     view was seeded, has not cut and so did not prove. The workers
#     waiting for it hold units, the queue runs dry and never closes: the
#     pass hangs. FIX "none" is that design and fails R2. FIX "release"
#     lets the waiters go without a proof: they seed in part, and R3
#     fails. FIX "whole" is the one kept: a prober that merges without
#     having cut says views are to be whole, then lets the waiters go.
#     pool.go was "none" when this was written; the test
#     TestProbeThatCutsNothingLetsGo pins "whole".
# D3: with views kept between runs a view seeded in part may lack
#     nothing, and who probes and who waits was settled before the view
#     was there to look at. A prober whose view lacks nothing cuts, merges
#     and lets the waiters go, having shown nothing of views that do lack
#     blobs: two of them then cut unproven. ORDER "decide_first" is that
#     design and fails R3 with three workers behind the first. The one
#     kept, "seed_first", gets the view first: only one that lacks blobs
#     probes or waits, and one that lacks none just cuts. The waiters'
#     views are seeded while the probe cuts, not after. The test
#     TestKeptViewLackingNothingDoesNotProbe pins it.
# D2: a oneof assigned straight to a field of a record in a list
#     (workers[i].outcome = oneof KINDS) does not reach the record in
#     fizzbee 0.5.4. It goes through a local.
#
# mutation runs, each a change to the model and the assertion that then
# fails; the first five are MUTANT values, the rest edits of a copy:
#   no_retry         a failed cut in a thin view is not cut again    R1 ResultIsTheUnitsOwn
#   retry_forgets    the second cut says ok whatever the first said  R1 ResultIsTheUnitsOwn
#   no_complete      a view is not made whole before a cut           R5 NoThinCutOnceWholeSeen
#   no_merge_whole   a merge finding a blob fetched again is silent  R4 ColdProbeSeedsNoOtherThin
#   close_first      probed is closed before whole is said           R4 ColdProbeSeedsNoOtherThin
#   a fetch leaves no mark for the merge (and R4 off)                R6 OneDirtyCutAWorker
#   a unit is skipped though its group goes on                       R7 SkippedOnlyWhenStopped
#   whole is unsaid at the end                                       R7 WholeStays
#   a unit is queued a second time                                   R1 HandedOnOnce
#   the units after a lead are never queued                          R1 EveryUnitAccountedFor
#   FIX "none"                                                       R2, as a deadlock
#   FIX "release"                                                    R3 OneThinViewUntilProven
#   ORDER "decide_first" (kept4)                                     R3 OneThinViewUntilProven

W = 3            # workers, the first without a view
GROUPS = [1, 1]  # per group, the units after its lead
KINDS = ["ok", "bad"]
MAX_STOPS = 0
FIX = "whole"    # or "none", "release"
MUTANT = ""      # for the mutation runs: no_retry, no_complete, no_merge_whole,
                 # retry_forgets, close_first

NEEDS = ["recent", "old"]
SEEDS = ["thin"]         # what seeding in part gives: with "whole" too, a
                         # kept view that lacks nothing
ORDER = "seed_first"     # or "decide_first"

# plan is every unit as (group, is the lead).
def plan(groups):
    out = []
    for g in range(len(groups)):
        for k in range(groups[g] + 1):
            out.append((g, k == 0))
    return out

def movable(w, queue, closed, probed):
    if w.pc == "idle":
        return len(queue) > 0 or closed
    if w.pc == "wait":
        return probed == "closed"
    return w.pc != "exit"

def all_exit(workers):
    return len([w for w in workers if w.pc != "exit"]) == 0

action Init:
    # state: new, taken, cut (handed on), skipped
    units = [record(g=x[0], lead=x[1], state="new") for x in plan(GROUPS)]
    # outcome is what the worker's chisel last said: "", ok, bad, missing
    workers = [record(pc="idle", item=-1, isolate=(i > 0), view="none", probe=False, was_probe=False,
                      cuts=False, cut_thin=False, pending=False, refetched=False, outcome="", own="", let_go=False,
                      owes_whole=False, dirty=0) for i in range(W)]
    queue = [u for u in range(len(units)) if units[u].lead]
    closed = False
    pending = len(GROUPS)
    stopped = [False for g in GROUPS]
    lead_stopped = [False for g in GROUPS]   # the group's lead was what stopped it
    stops = 0
    whole = False
    probed = "nil"       # nil, open, closed
    # witnesses: each stays as it is in a model that keeps its requirement
    handed = [False for x in units]   # per unit: it reached the caller
    handed_twice = False       # a unit reached the caller a second time
    missing_handed_on = False  # a failure for a lacking blob reached the caller
    own_lost = False           # a unit's own failure did not reach the caller
    thin_made = 0              # views seeded in part
    probe_dirty = False        # the probing view's first cut lacked a blob, whenever it came
    proven = False             # a view seeded in part has cut a unit and merged
    late_thin_cut = False      # a cut in a thin view by a worker that had seen whole

atomic fair action Step:
    i = oneof [j for j in range(W) if movable(workers[j], queue, closed, probed)]
    pc = workers[i].pc
    u = workers[i].item
    if pc == "idle":
        if len(queue) > 0:
            workers[i].item = queue[0]
            units[queue[0]].state = "taken"
            queue = queue[1:]
            if workers[i].isolate:
                workers[i].pc = "prepare"
            else:
                workers[i].pc = "skipcheck"
        else:
            workers[i].pc = "close"
    elif pc == "prepare":
        workers[i].isolate = False
        if ORDER == "decide_first":
            # the design before views were kept: who probes and who waits
            # is settled before the view is there to look at
            if whole:
                workers[i].view = "whole"
                workers[i].pc = "skipcheck"
            elif probed == "nil":
                probed = "open"
                workers[i].probe = True
                workers[i].was_probe = True
                got = oneof SEEDS
                workers[i].view = got
                if got == "thin":
                    thin_made = thin_made + 1
                workers[i].pc = "skipcheck"
            else:
                workers[i].pc = "wait"
        else:
            # the view first: seeded, or a kept one taken and brought up
            # to date, whole when views are to be
            got = "whole"
            if not whole:
                got = oneof SEEDS
            workers[i].view = got
            if got == "thin":
                workers[i].pc = "gate"
            else:
                workers[i].pc = "skipcheck"
    elif pc == "gate":
        # only a view seeded in part probes or waits
        if whole:
            workers[i].view = "whole"
            workers[i].pc = "skipcheck"
        elif probed == "nil":
            probed = "open"
            workers[i].probe = True
            workers[i].was_probe = True
            thin_made = thin_made + 1
            workers[i].pc = "skipcheck"
        else:
            workers[i].pc = "wait"
    elif pc == "wait":
        if whole:
            workers[i].view = "whole"
        elif ORDER == "decide_first":
            got = oneof SEEDS
            workers[i].view = got
            if got == "thin":
                thin_made = thin_made + 1
        else:
            thin_made = thin_made + 1
        workers[i].pc = "skipcheck"
    elif pc == "skipcheck":
        if stopped[units[u].g]:
            units[u].state = "skipped"
            if workers[i].view == "none":
                workers[i].pc = "enditem"
            else:
                workers[i].pc = "merge"
        elif workers[i].view == "thin":
            workers[i].pc = "cut"
        else:
            workers[i].cuts = True
            workers[i].outcome = "ok"
            workers[i].pc = "done"
    elif pc == "cut":
        saw_whole = whole
        if saw_whole and MUTANT != "no_complete":
            workers[i].view = "whole"
        first = not workers[i].cuts
        workers[i].cuts = True
        outcome = "ok"
        if workers[i].view == "thin":
            workers[i].cut_thin = True
            if saw_whole:
                late_thin_cut = True
            outcome = oneof KINDS
            needs = oneof NEEDS
            if needs == "old":
                workers[i].dirty = workers[i].dirty + 1
                if workers[i].was_probe and first:
                    probe_dirty = True
                net_up = oneof [True, False]
                if net_up:
                    workers[i].pending = True
                else:
                    outcome = "missing"
        workers[i].outcome = outcome
        if outcome == "bad":
            workers[i].own = "bad"
        if workers[i].view == "thin" and outcome != "ok" and MUTANT != "no_retry":
            workers[i].pc = "retry"
        else:
            workers[i].pc = "done"
    elif pc == "retry":
        whole = True
        workers[i].view = "whole"
        # Complete links in what was fetched again: the merge no longer
        # sees it. In the whole view the unit's own outcome is what is left.
        workers[i].pending = False
        if workers[i].outcome == "missing":
            # through a local: a oneof assigned straight to a record's
            # field does not reach the record
            own = oneof KINDS
            workers[i].outcome = own
        if MUTANT == "retry_forgets":
            workers[i].outcome = "ok"
        workers[i].pc = "done"
    elif pc == "done":
        if handed[u]:
            handed_twice = True
        handed[u] = True
        units[u].state = "cut"
        if workers[i].outcome == "missing":
            missing_handed_on = True
        if workers[i].own == "bad" and workers[i].outcome != "bad":
            own_lost = True
        workers[i].outcome = ""
        workers[i].own = ""
        stop = oneof ([False, True] if stops < MAX_STOPS else [False])
        if stop:
            stopped[units[u].g] = True
            stops = stops + 1
            if units[u].lead:
                lead_stopped[units[u].g] = True
        if workers[i].view == "none":
            workers[i].pc = "enditem"
        else:
            workers[i].pc = "merge"
    elif pc == "merge":
        if workers[i].pending:
            workers[i].pending = False
            workers[i].refetched = True
        say_whole = False
        if workers[i].refetched and MUTANT != "no_merge_whole":
            say_whole = True
        if FIX == "whole" and workers[i].probe and not workers[i].cuts:
            say_whole = True
        # A view seeded in part has cut and merged: the proof, whoever
        # closes the channel and whenever.
        if workers[i].probe and workers[i].cut_thin:
            proven = True
        if MUTANT == "close_first":
            # the channel closed here, whole only said at the next step
            workers[i].owes_whole = say_whole
            if workers[i].probe and (workers[i].cuts or FIX != "none"):
                if not workers[i].cuts:
                    workers[i].let_go = True
                workers[i].probe = False
                probed = "closed"
        elif say_whole:
            whole = True
        workers[i].pc = "enditem"
    elif pc == "enditem":
        if workers[i].owes_whole:
            workers[i].owes_whole = False
            whole = True
        if workers[i].probe:
            if workers[i].cuts:
                workers[i].probe = False
                probed = "closed"
            elif FIX != "none":
                workers[i].probe = False
                workers[i].let_go = True
                probed = "closed"
        if units[u].lead and not stopped[units[u].g]:
            rest = [r for r in range(len(units)) if units[r].g == units[u].g and not units[r].lead]
            queue = queue + rest
            pending = pending + len(rest)
        pending = pending - 1
        if pending == 0:
            closed = True
        workers[i].item = -1
        workers[i].pc = "idle"
    elif pc == "close":
        if workers[i].refetched:
            whole = True
        if workers[i].probe:
            workers[i].probe = False
            probed = "closed"
            if not workers[i].cuts:
                workers[i].let_go = True
        workers[i].pc = "exit"

# The end of the pass is a state like any other, with a step of its own, so
# a state that cannot move is one the checker reports.
atomic action Finished:
    require all_exit(workers)
    pass

# R1: never a failure for a blob the view lacked, and a failure of the
# unit's own is the one handed on.
always assertion ResultIsTheUnitsOwn:
    return not missing_handed_on and not own_lost

# R1: once, and a unit is "cut" just when it was handed on.
always assertion HandedOnOnce:
    if handed_twice:
        return False
    for x in range(len(units)):
        if units[x].state == "cut" and not handed[x]:
            return False
        if handed[x] and units[x].state != "cut":
            return False
    return True

# R1, at the end: every unit was cut, skipped, or never queued since its
# group's lead stopped the group.
always assertion EveryUnitAccountedFor:
    if not all_exit(workers):
        return True
    for x in units:
        if x.state == "taken":
            return False
        if x.state == "new" and (x.lead or not lead_stopped[x.g]):
            return False
    return True

# R2
always eventually assertion PassEnds:
    return all_exit(workers)

# R3
always assertion OneThinViewUntilProven:
    return proven or thin_made <= 1

# R4
always assertion ColdProbeSeedsNoOtherThin:
    return not probe_dirty or thin_made == 1

# R5
always assertion NoThinCutOnceWholeSeen:
    return not late_thin_cut

# R6
always assertion OneDirtyCutAWorker:
    for w in workers:
        if w.dirty > 1:
            return False
    return True

# R7
always assertion SkippedOnlyWhenStopped:
    for x in units:
        if x.state == "skipped" and not stopped[x.g]:
            return False
    return True

# R7
transition assertion WholeStays(before, after):
    if before.whole and not after.whole:
        return False
    if before.probed == "closed" and after.probed != "closed":
        return False
    return True

# coverage: each branch of the protocol is taken somewhere, and each
# property's "if" comes true somewhere. Each names the state at the moment
# of the event, or a mark the event alone leaves.
# these three need a cut that lacks an old blob, so only where one may
exists assertion ACutIsCutAgain:
    return "old" not in NEEDS or len([w for w in workers if w.pc == "retry"]) > 0

exists assertion AnOwnFailureIsCutAgain:
    return len(KINDS) == 1 or len([w for w in workers if w.pc == "retry" and w.own == "bad"]) > 0

exists assertion AMergeMakesViewsWhole:
    return "old" not in NEEDS or whole and len([w for w in workers if w.refetched and w.pc == "enditem"]) > 0

exists assertion TwoThinViews:
    return thin_made == 2

exists assertion AColdProbe:
    return "old" not in NEEDS or probe_dirty

exists assertion ACleanCutInAThinView:
    return len([w for w in workers if w.pc == "done" and w.view == "thin" and w.outcome == "ok" and not w.pending]) > 0

# the three that need a group stopped, so only where one may be
exists assertion AUnitIsSkipped:
    return MAX_STOPS == 0 or len([x for x in units if x.state == "skipped"]) > 0

exists assertion TheProberLetsGoUnproven:
    return MAX_STOPS == 0 or len([w for w in workers if w.let_go]) > 0

# and this one a unit left to cut in another group
exists assertion TheProberThatLetGoCutsLater:
    return MAX_STOPS == 0 or GROUPS[len(GROUPS) - 1] == 0 or len([w for w in workers if w.let_go and w.cuts]) > 0

# a kept view lacking nothing cuts beside a probe not yet proven
exists assertion AKeptViewSkipsTheProbe:
    return "whole" not in SEEDS or ORDER != "seed_first" or len([w for w in workers if w.pc == "done" and w.view == "whole" and not w.was_probe]) > 0 and not proven and not whole and probed == "open"

exists assertion AProberProves:
    return proven

exists assertion APassEndsWithEveryUnitCut:
    return all_exit(workers) and len([x for x in units if x.state != "cut"]) == 0
